              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "Depending on whether you are looking for a **button-down** shirt or a **T-shirt/hoodie** style, the thin Columbia PFG (Performance Fishing Gear) shirts are called:\n\n### 1. The Button-Down Style: **The Tamiami (or Tamiami II / Super Tamiami)**\nIf you are looking for the classic, short or long-sleeved button-up fishing shirt that feels incredibly lightweight and whisper-thin, you are looking for the **Tamiami**. \n* **The Fabric:** It is made of 100% ultra-light polyester ripstop. \n* **Why it feels thin:** Unlike Columbia\u2019s heavier cotton shirts (like the *Bonehead*) or their stiffer, heavier nylon shirts (like the *Bahama*), the Tamiami is highly breathable, incredibly soft, and extremely thin. It also features built-in mesh-lined vents on the back to keep you cool.\n\n### 2. The T-Shirt / Hoodie Style: **The Terminal Tackle**\nIf you are looking for the silky, stretchy, ultra-thin athletic long-sleeve shirt (often with a hood or a crew neck) that people wear for sun protection, you are looking for the **Terminal Tackle**.\n* **The Fabric:** It is made of a thin, smooth, and stretchy 100% polyester interlock fabric. \n* **Why it feels thin:** It is designed to act as a second skin that blocks 98% of the sun's rays (UPF 50) while staying cool, dry, and weightless. It is highly popular not just for fishing, but also for hiking, yard work, and beach days.",
